        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey\n- Structures: Endem TV Tower, Cagaloglu Hamam\n- Concepts: revolving restaurant, public hamam, library funding\n\nFacts:\n- Cagaloglu Hamam in Istanbul, Turkey, was built in 1741.\n- Cagaloglu Hamam was the last public hamam of its kind.\n- Cagaloglu Hamam was built to raise revenue for a library.\n- Endem TV Tower in Istanbul, Turkey, is 257 meters tall.\n- Endem TV Tower once included a revolving restaurant 154 meters above the ground.",
