        "original_id": "32583ed9-d32d-585f-8be8-ff7047971b1d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beylikdüzü, Istanbul, Turkey, Eminönü, Alemdar, Hilal-i Ahmer Street, Ayasofya\n- Structures: Endem TV Tower, Cağaloğlu Hamam\n- People: Sultan Mahmud I\n- Concepts: Ottoman Empire, public hamams, observation decks, revolving restaurants\n\nFacts:\n- Cağaloğlu Hamam was finished in 1741 in Eminönü, Alemdar, on Hilal-i Ahmer Street in Istanbul.\n- Cağaloğlu Hamam was built as a public hamam to raise revenue for the library of Sultan Mahmud I, which had previously been situated inside the mosque of Ayasofya.\n- Cağaloğlu Hamam was the last hamam built in the Ottoman Empire and the last example of its kind built in Istanbul, and it is still operational.\n- Endem TV Tower in Beylikdüzü, Istanbul, Turkey, was built between 1998 and 2002.\n- Endem TV Tower has a total height of 257 meters including its antenna.\n- Endem TV Tower has a now closed revolving restaurant 154 meters above ground and an observation deck at 160 meters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cf3b73a9-9886-5523-ba53-fff8915db328",
        "text": "Page: Endem TV Tower. Sentence: Endem TV Tower is a TV tower in Beylikdüzü, Istanbul, Turkey.\nPage: Endem TV Tower. Sentence: It was built between 1998 and 2002, and has a now closed revolving restaurant 154 m above ground, as well as an observation deck at 160 m .\nPage: Endem TV Tower. Sentence: The total height of the tower si 257 m including the antenna.\nPage: Cağaloğlu Hamam. Sentence: The Cağaloğlu Hamam, finished in 1741, is the last hamam to be built in the Ottoman Empire.\nPage: Cağaloğlu Hamam. Sentence: It was constructed in Istanbul Eminönü, in Alemdar, on Hilal-i Ahmer street as a public hamam to raise revenue for the library of Sultan Mahmud I, previously situated inside the mosque of Ayasofya.\nPage: Cağaloğlu Hamam. Sentence: It is the last example of its kind to be built in Istanbul and is still operational today.",
